         <packagedElement xmi:id="xsd.XMLSchema"
                           xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#XMLSchema"
                           xmi:type="uml:Package">
            <ownedComment xmi:id="xsd.XMLSchema-ownedComment"
                           xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#XMLSchema-ownedComment"
                           xmi:type="uml:Comment">
               <body>XML Schema: Datatypes is part 2 of the specification of the XML Schema language.
See: https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/.</body>
               <annotatedElement xmi:idref="xsd.XMLSchema"/>
            </ownedComment>
            <name>XMLSchema</name>
            <URI>http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#</URI>
            <packagedElement xmi:id="xsd.anyURI"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI"
                              xmi:type="uml:DataType">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="xsd.anyURI-ownedComment"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI-ownedComment"
                              xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <body>Definition
==========
Definition from XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition:
"anyURI" represents a Uniform Resource Identifier Reference (URI). An "anyURI" value can be absolute or relative, and may have an optional fragment identifier (i.e., it may be a URI Reference). This type should be used to specify the intention that the value fulfills the role of a URI as defined by [RFC 2396], as amended by [RFC 2732]. For details see https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#anyURI.</body>
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="xsd.anyURI"/>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>anyURI</name>
            </packagedElement>
            <packagedElement xmi:id="xsd.date"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date"
                              xmi:type="uml:DataType">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="xsd.date-ownedComment"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date-ownedComment"
                              xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <body>Definition
==========
Definition from XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition:
"The value space of date consists of top-open intervals of exactly one day in length on the timelines of dateTime, beginning on the beginning moment of each day (in each timezone), i.e. '00:00:00', up to but not including '24:00:00' (which is identical with '00:00:00' of the next day). For nontimezoned values, the top-open intervals disjointly cover the nontimezoned timeline, one per day. For timezoned values, the intervals begin at every minute and therefore overlap." For details see https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#date.</body>
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="xsd.date"/>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>date</name>
            </packagedElement>
            <packagedElement xmi:id="xsd.language"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#language"
                              xmi:type="uml:DataType">
               <ownedComment xmi:id="xsd.language-ownedComment"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#language-ownedComment"
                              xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                  <body>Definition
==========
Definition from XML Schema Part 2: Datatypes Second Edition:
"language" represents natural language identifiers as defined by by [RFC 3066]. The value space of "language" is the set of all strings that are valid language identifiers as defined [RFC 3066] . The lexical space of language is the set of all strings that conform to the pattern [a-zA-Z]{1,8}(-[a-zA-Z0-9]{1,8})*. The base type of "language" is token. https://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#language.</body>
                  <annotatedElement xmi:idref="xsd.language"/>
               </ownedComment>
               <name>language</name>
            </packagedElement>
            <packagedElement xmi:id="xsd.PackageInformation"
                              xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#PackageInformation"
                              xmi:type="uml:DataType">
               <name>PackageInformation</name>
               <ownedAttribute xmi:id="xsd.PackageInformation-prefix"
                                xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#PackageInformation-prefix"
                                xmi:type="uml:Property">
                  <name>prefix</name>
                  <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                         href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
                  <defaultValue xmi:id="xsd.PackageInformation-prefix-defaultValue"
                                 xmi:uuid="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#PackageInformation-prefix-defaultValue"
                                 xmi:type="uml:LiteralString">
                     <value>xsd</value>
                  </defaultValue>
               </ownedAttribute>
            </packagedElement>
