               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.CategorySet"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CategorySet"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.CategorySet-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CategorySet-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
Concept system where the underlying concepts are categories.

Examples
==========
"Male" and "Female" categories in a category set named "Gender".

Explanatory notes
===================
The categories in a category set help define the meaning of the category set. Gender can be defined as "male or female" - see example above. A category set can be used directly by questions to express a set of response choices.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CategorySet"/>
