               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ConceptSystemCorrespondence"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConceptSystemCorrespondence"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ConceptSystemCorrespondence-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConceptSystemCorrespondence-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Relationship between 2 or more concept systems described through mapping similarity relationships between their member concepts.  

Examples 
========== 
Correspondence between the concepts used to define the amount of salt dissolved in a body of water: the concepts "salinity" and "saltiness" might be described as equivalent, for example.

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Describes correspondence with one or more maps which identify a source and target concept and defines their commonality and difference using descriptive text and controlled vocabularies.</body>
