                        </upperValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.ReferenceValue_correspondsTo_VariableValueComponent"/>
                     </ownedEnd>
                     <memberEnd xmi:idref="cdi.ReferenceValue-ownedAttribute-1"/>
                     <memberEnd xmi:idref="cdi.correspondsTo-ownedEnd-ReferenceValue"/>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.AttributeComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AttributeComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.AttributeComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AttributeComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a data structure to qualify observations or provide other types of supplementary information.  

Examples 
========== 
The publication status of an observation (e.g. provisional, final, revised).</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.AttributeComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>AttributeComponent</name>
                     <generalization xmi:id="cdi.AttributeComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AttributeComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                        <general xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </generalization>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.AttributeComponent-ownedAttribute-1"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AttributeComponent-ownedAttribute-1"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.AttributeComponent-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AttributeComponent-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.AttributeComponent-ownedAttribute-1-upperValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AttributeComponent-ownedAttribute-1-upperValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                           <value>*</value>
                        </upperValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.AttributeComponent_qualifies_DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Indexes the components in a data structure using integers with a position indicated by incrementing upward from 0 or 1.</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ComponentPosition"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>ComponentPosition</name>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition-identifier"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition-identifier"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>identifier</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition-value"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition-value"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>value</name>
                        <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                               href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#Integer"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition-ownedAttribute-3"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition-ownedAttribute-3"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ComponentPosition-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ComponentPosition-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.ComponentPosition_indexes_DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a data structure.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
A represented variable can have different roles in different data structures. For instance, the variable sex can be a measure in a wide data structure and a dimension in a dimensional data structure.</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>DataStructureComponent</name>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-identifier"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-identifier"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>identifier</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-semantic"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-semantic"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>semantic</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-semantic-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-semantic-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-semantic-upperValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-semantic-upperValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                           <value>*</value>
                        </upperValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-specialization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-specialization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>specialization</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.SpecializationRole"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-specialization-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-specialization-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-ownedAttribute-4"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-ownedAttribute-4"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.RepresentedVariable"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.DataStructureComponent-ownedAttribute-4-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DataStructureComponent-ownedAttribute-4-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent_isDefinedBy_RepresentedVariable"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a dimensional data structure to identify the universes associated with data points. The variable acts as a field in the compound identifier (the key structure) to disambiguate the cells in the multi-dimensional "cube".  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
The categories from each dimension often are used in combination to identify a cell. The meaning of the combination of the categories supplies meaning to the cell.</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.DimensionComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>DimensionComponent</name>
                     <generalization xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                        <general xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </generalization>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-categoricalAdditivity"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-categoricalAdditivity"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>categoricalAdditivity</name>
                        <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                               href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#Boolean"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-categoricalAdditivity-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-categoricalAdditivity-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <defaultValue xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-categoricalAdditivity-defaultValue"
                                       xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-categoricalAdditivity-defaultValue"
                                       xmi:type="uml:LiteralBoolean">
                           <value>False</value>
                        </defaultValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.ValueDomain"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.DimensionComponent-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DimensionComponent-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.DimensionComponent_isStructuredBy_ValueDomain"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKey"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKey"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKey-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKey-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition
============
Role of a set of data structure components for content referencing purposes

Explanatory notes
===================
Equivalent to foreign key in the relational model.
It can be used in conjunction with primary key to link data structures and their related data sets.
</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ForeignKey"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>ForeignKey</name>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKey-identifier"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKey-identifier"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>identifier</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKey-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKey-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKey-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKey-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent"/>
                        <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKey-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKey-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                           <value>*</value>
                        </upperValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent_isComposedOf_ForeignKey"/>
                        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKeyComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKeyComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition
============
Role of a data structure component for content referencing purposes

Explanatory notes
===================
Equivalent to a foreign key attribute (i.e. column) in the relational model.
It can be used in conjunction with a primary key component to link data structures and their related data sets.
</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>ForeignKeyComponent</name>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent-identifier"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKeyComponent-identifier"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>identifier</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKeyComponent-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKeyComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent"/>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent_references_PrimaryKeyComponent"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent-ownedAttribute-3"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ForeignKeyComponent-ownedAttribute-3"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.ForeignKeyComponent_correspondsTo_DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.IdentifierComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#IdentifierComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.IdentifierComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#IdentifierComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a long or wide data structure to identify the units associated to data points, and in dimensional and key value data structures to provide identifying fields for the instance values.  

Examples 
========== 
The personal identification number of a Swedish citizen for unit data or the name of a country in the European Union for dimensional data.




</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.IdentifierComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>IdentifierComponent</name>
                     <generalization xmi:id="cdi.IdentifierComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#IdentifierComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                        <general xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </generalization>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.MeasureComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#MeasureComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.MeasureComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#MeasureComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a data structure to hold the observed/derived values.  

Examples 
========== 
Height of a person in a wide or long dataset or number of citizens in a country in a dataset for multiple countries (dimensional dataset).  
</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.MeasureComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>MeasureComponent</name>
                     <generalization xmi:id="cdi.MeasureComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#MeasureComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                        <general xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </generalization>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.MeasureComponent-name"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#MeasureComponent-name"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>name</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.ObjectName"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.MeasureComponent-name-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#MeasureComponent-name-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.MeasureComponent-name-upperValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#MeasureComponent-name-upperValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                           <value>*</value>
                        </upperValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKey"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKey"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKey-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKey-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition
============
Role of a set of data structure components for content linkage purposes

Explanatory notes
===================
Equivalent to primary key in the relational model.
A primary key essentially indicates which data structure components correspond to key members.
It can also be used in conjunction with foreign key to link data structures and their related datasets.</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.PrimaryKey"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>PrimaryKey</name>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKey-identifier"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKey-identifier"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>identifier</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKey-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKey-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKey-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKey-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent"/>
                        <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKey-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKey-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                           <value>*</value>
                        </upperValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent_isComposedOf_PrimaryKey"/>
                        <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKeyComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKeyComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition
============
Role of a data structure component for content identification purposes

Explanatory notes
===================
Equivalent to a primary key attribute (i.e. column) in the relational model.
It can be used in conjunction with a foreign key component to link data structures and their related datasets.
</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>PrimaryKeyComponent</name>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent-identifier"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKeyComponent-identifier"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <name>identifier</name>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKeyComponent-identifier-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PrimaryKeyComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.PrimaryKeyComponent_correspondsTo_DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableDescriptorComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a data structure to provide codes for variable identification.   

Examples 
========== 
Consider {"income", "age"} to be the value domain of the represented variable working as a variable descriptor component.  The two codes, i.e. those designating "income" and "age", are descriptors used to identify which values in the variable value component correspond to income and which ones to age.   

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Whenever more than one variable appears in the same column, we need a mechanism to distinguish which values correspond to which variable. This mechanism is provided by the variable descriptor component, which contains the codes used to link the variables to their values.  This structure provides a flexible mechanism avoiding the need for a formal pointer.</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>VariableDescriptorComponent</name>
                     <generalization xmi:id="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableDescriptorComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                        <general xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </generalization>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedAttribute-1"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedAttribute-1"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.DescriptorVariable"/>
                        <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                     xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                           <value>0</value>
                        </lowerValue>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent_isDefinedBy_DescriptorVariable"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                     <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableDescriptorComponent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Property">
                        <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                        <type xmi:idref="cdi.VariableValueComponent"/>
                        <association xmi:idref="cdi.VariableDescriptorComponent_refersTo_VariableValueComponent"/>
                     </ownedAttribute>
                  </packagedElement>
                  <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.VariableValueComponent"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableValueComponent"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Class">
                     <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.VariableValueComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableValueComponent-ownedComment"
                                    xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                        <body>Definition 
============ 
Role given to a represented variable in the context of a data structure to record values of multiple variables.   

Examples 
========== 
Consider two variables, i.e. income and age, with their values living together in different entries in the same column.  The values of those two variables are now in the value domain of a single variable (the one working as a variable value component).  Another column, based on a variable descriptor component, use codes for "income" and "age" to distinguish income values from age values.   

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
A variable value component captures the values of multiple variables that have been transposed into a single column.  The variable descriptor component provides a mechanism to identify which of those values correspond to which variable.   This structure provides a flexible mechanism avoiding the need for a formal pointer.
</body>
                        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.VariableValueComponent"/>
                     </ownedComment>
                     <name>VariableValueComponent</name>
                     <generalization xmi:id="cdi.VariableValueComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#VariableValueComponent-generalization"
                                      xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                        <general xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructureComponent"/>
                     </generalization>
                  </packagedElement>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Dimensional"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Dimensional"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Package">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Dimensional-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Dimensional-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>This package contains the classes which are used to define multi-dimensional data structures (i.e., data cubes). It is important to note that the logical treatment of data as a multi-dimensional structure does not necessarily dictate a particular physical format for the data.</body>
