                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Activity-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Task described at a conceptual level. It is not parameterized and as such is less reusable. For more logical/physical, fine-grained, reusable description there is a sub-type called step.  

Examples 
========== 
Phases and sub-processes of the Generic Statistical Business Process Model (GSBPM) are examples of activity.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
An activity is invoked by control logic. It may use and/or produce information objects referenced with the entityUsed and entityProduced attributes.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Activity"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Activity</name>
