               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.AllenIntervalAlgebra"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AllenIntervalAlgebra"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.AllenIntervalAlgebra-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AllenIntervalAlgebra-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
==========
Control logic where the execution flow is determined by the satisfaction of temporal constraints specified with Allen's Interval Algebra over time intervals. Allen's interval algebra consists of thirteen temporal interval relations and the operations defined on them. Together these relations are distinct (any pair of definite intervals are described by one and only one of the relations), exhaustive (any pair of definite intervals are described by one of the relations), and qualitative (no numeric time spans are considered). See https://www.ics.uci.edu/~alspaugh/cls/shr/allen.html.

Examples
========
An Allen overlap indicates that within a sequence two procedures overlap in time. 

Explanatory notes
=================
Allen's intervals are pairwise.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.AllenIntervalAlgebra"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>AllenIntervalAlgebra</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.AllenIntervalAlgebra-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AllenIntervalAlgebra-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.TemporalConstraints"/>
                  </generalization>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.AllenIntervalAlgebra-temporalIntervalRelation"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#AllenIntervalAlgebra-temporalIntervalRelation"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>temporalIntervalRelation</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.TemporalRelation"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConditionalControlLogic"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConditionalControlLogic-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
A set of decision points which determine the flow between the steps used to perform an activity. 

Examples 
========== 
Loop, IfThenElse, RepeatWhile, etc. </body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>ConditionalControlLogic</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConditionalControlLogic-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.DeterministicImperative"/>
                  </generalization>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic-condition"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConditionalControlLogic-condition"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>condition</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.CommandCode"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic-construct"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ConditionalControlLogic-construct"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>construct</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ControlConstruct"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ControlLogic"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ControlLogic"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ControlLogic-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ControlLogic-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Program in which the order of statements is explicit. Control logic is either deterministic (imperative) or non-deterministic (declarative). Deterministic control logic consists of control constructs. Declarative control logic is constraint- and/or rule-based. Control logic may contain control logic.  

Examples 
========== 
A loop control construct is deterministic control logic. A script is deterministic control logic. Rule based scheduling is declarative control logic.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
DDI-CDI has extended control logic to include non-deterministic activity and step controls, which are not specifically described in DDI Lifecycle or DDI Codebook.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ControlLogic"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>ControlLogic</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ControlLogic-description"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ControlLogic-description"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>description</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ControlLogic-description-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ControlLogic-description-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ControlLogic-displayLabel"
