               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Curator"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Curator"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Curator-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Curator-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Curator is a software agent that uses techniques such as natural language processing to map facts in the research data store to the condition part of a rule.  

Examples 
========== 
Domain-specific curators are available as both open source and commercial products.   

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
The curator assists in identifying the rules that are currently in play in the rule set.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Curator"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Curator</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.Curator-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Curator-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.ProcessingAgent"/>
                  </generalization>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.DeterministicImperative"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DeterministicImperative"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.DeterministicImperative-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DeterministicImperative-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Deterministic imperative is a subtype of control logic. Deterministic control logic consists of control constructs.   

Examples 
========== 
A Loop control construct is deterministic control logic. A script is deterministic control logic.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Because control logic covers both deterministic and non-deterministic forms, it has been divided into the appropriate subtypes.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.DeterministicImperative"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>DeterministicImperative</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.DeterministicImperative-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#DeterministicImperative-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.ControlLogic"/>
                  </generalization>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Relationships between parameters across steps is described by the information flow definition. Each relationship creates a pathway for an information object to follow.  

Examples 
========== 
The output of one parameter might be the input of another one. Think of a Business Process Model and Notation (BPMN) diagram or an extract, transform, and load (ETL) pipeline definition as the sum of these relationships.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
In DDI Lifecycle an information flow definition was referred to in terms of a "binding".</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>InformationFlowDefinition</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Parameter"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition_from_Parameter"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Parameter"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-3-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#InformationFlowDefinition-ownedAttribute-3-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.InformationFlowDefinition_to_Parameter"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.NonDeterministicDeclarative"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#NonDeterministicDeclarative"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.NonDeterministicDeclarative-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#NonDeterministicDeclarative-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Non-deterministic control logic is a subtype of control logic. Non-deterministic (or declarative) control logic is constraint- and/or rule-based.  

Examples 
========== 
Rule based scheduling is declarative control logic.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Unlike DDI Lifecycle, DDI-CDI describes non-deterministic activity and step controls.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.NonDeterministicDeclarative"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>NonDeterministicDeclarative</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.NonDeterministicDeclarative-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#NonDeterministicDeclarative-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.ControlLogic"/>
                  </generalization>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Parameter"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Input or output to control logic and the step/sub-step it invokes. Parameters may take the form of any information object, including data sets and structured metadata as well as configuration information for the step/sub-step.  

Examples 
========== 
A dimensional data set; a long data structure.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Parameter"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Parameter</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-entityBound"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-entityBound"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>entityBound</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Reference"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-entityBound-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-entityBound-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-entityBound-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-entityBound-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-name"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-name"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>name</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ObjectName"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-name-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-name-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.Parameter-name-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Parameter-name-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
A processing agent orchestrates the production of information objects in a production environment. There are processing agents which perform data capture, data editing/processing, and data analysis (etc.), each in the appropriate production environments. The processing agent performs an activity based on the control logic.  

Examples 
========== 
A processing agent initiates a data capture sequence, obtaining readings from a sensor. A processing agent initiates rule based scheduling. A processing agent is informed by control logic to invoke an imputation activity.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ProcessingAgent"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>ProcessingAgent</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.Agent"/>
                  </generalization>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-1"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-1"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Activity"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-1-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-1-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.ProcessingAgent_performs_Activity"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ProductionEnvironment"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProcessingAgent-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.ProcessingAgent_operatesOn_ProductionEnvironment"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Production environments consume and produce information objects by way of processing pipelines orchestrated by the processing agent.  

Examples 
========== 
Data processing platforms and data analysis platforms are types of production environments. Each of these platforms may have subtypes.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.ProductionEnvironment"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>ProductionEnvironment</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-description"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-description"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>description</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-description-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-description-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-displayLabel"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-displayLabel"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>displayLabel</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.LabelForDisplay"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-displayLabel-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-displayLabel-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-displayLabel-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-displayLabel-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-name"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-name"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>name</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ObjectName"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-name-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-name-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.ProductionEnvironment-name-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ProductionEnvironment-name-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Rule"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Rule-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
A rule has a condition part and an action part. A rule takes the form of: If [Condition} Then [Action]. A rule belongs to a rule set which is a component of rule based scheduling performed by the processing agent  

Examples 
========== 
If Exists [InformationObject] Then Perform [Activity]  </body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Rule"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Rule</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Rule-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Rule-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Rule-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ConditionalControlLogic"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Rule-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.Rule-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Rule-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.Rule_hasPrecondition_ConditionalControlLogic"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Rule based scheduling performs a fact check on rules from the rule set, testing their condition part against the facts in the research data store. Fact checking may be assisted by a curator who can semantically compare the condition part of each candidate rule with the facts. The fact checker returns the next activity which rule based scheduling performs according to the following function: factcheck (RuleSet, ResearchDataStore, Curator): Activity.

Examples 
========== 
One real-life situation in which rule-based scheduling is performed involves data virtualization. Here the research datastore has a catalog of views available for use. Rule based scheduling might explore the catalog to determine the rule(s) in the rule set that currently apply. A software curator might assist in the decision in case there was no exact match between a rule and its condition(s) and given the current state of the research datastore. The curator typically uses natural language processing. 

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Rule based scheduling is guided by its scheduling strategy. This is described by an enumeration that consists of "forwardChaining" and "backwardChaining".
</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>RuleBasedScheduling</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.NonDeterministicDeclarative"/>
                  </generalization>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-schedulingType"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-schedulingType"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>schedulingType</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.SchedulingStrategy"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.RuleSet"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.RuleSet_has_RuleBasedScheduling"/>
                     <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Curator"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-3-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleBasedScheduling-ownedAttribute-3-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.Curator_has_RuleBasedScheduling"/>
                     <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
A rule set is a collection of rules. A rule set is a component of rule based scheduling.  

Examples 
========== 
If [A overlaps B] Then [X] If [B occurs before C] Then [Y] If [C equals D] Then [Z]  It might take a curator to understand what these rules mean in the context of a research data store.

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Rule based scheduling might have multiple rule sets each of which are domain-specific. The processing agent often helps with the selection of rule sets.
</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.RuleSet"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>RuleSet</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Rule"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.RuleSet-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#RuleSet-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.Rule_has_RuleSet"/>
                     <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Sequence"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Sequence"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Sequence-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Sequence-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
A sequence controls the order of activities or steps by defining a simple sequence. 

Examples 
========== 
A sequence might contain two subordinate sequences of activity - one for Round 1 activity of the research and the second for Round 2.

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
Unlike temporal constraints, sequence is NOT pairwise. However, a group of temporal constraints can specify an order with more precision than a sequence.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Sequence"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Sequence</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.Sequence-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Sequence-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.DeterministicImperative"/>
                  </generalization>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Sequence-ownedAttribute-1"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Sequence-ownedAttribute-1"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.SequencePosition"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Sequence-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Sequence-ownedAttribute-1-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.Sequence-ownedAttribute-1-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Sequence-ownedAttribute-1-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.SequencePosition_has_Sequence"/>
                     <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.SequencePosition"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#SequencePosition"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.SequencePosition-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#SequencePosition-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
Assigns a sequence number to an activity within a sequence.

</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.SequencePosition"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>SequencePosition</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.SequencePosition-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#SequencePosition-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.SequencePosition-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#SequencePosition-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.SequencePosition-value"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#SequencePosition-value"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>value</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#Integer"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.SequencePosition-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#SequencePosition-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Activity"/>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.SequencePosition_indexes_Activity"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Service"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Service"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Service-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Service-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Service is a type of processing agent. Services are atomic. They execute acts which have input and output parameters.  

Examples 
========== 
Given a location as input, a weather service provides weather data as output.  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
A service binds information objects to parameters at runtime.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Service"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Service</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.Service-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Service-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.ProcessingAgent"/>
                  </generalization>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Step"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Step"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Step-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Step-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
Reusable, parameterized activity associated to information flows. One or more steps perform an activity.

Examples
==========
An editing activity resolves into one or more steps. A transformation of a wide data set to a long data set takes a single step on an ETL (extract, transform, load) platform like Pentaho.

Explanatory notes
===================
Steps can be broken out into a sequence of sub steps ad infinitum.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Step"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Step</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.Step-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Step-generalization"
