               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.ClassificationStructure"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ClassificationStructure"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.ClassificationStructure-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#ClassificationStructure-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
Complex relation structure for use with statistical classification.  

Examples 
========== 
A classification structure for the International Standard Classification of Occupations (ISCO-08: https://www.ilo.org/public/english/bureau/stat/isco/isco08/) would describe each of the major classifications as a parent of its sub-classifications. 1 Managers, for example would be listed as a parent of four sub groups: 11 Chief Executives, Senior Officials and Legislators; 12 Chief Executives, Senior Officials and Legislators; 13 Production and Specialized Services Managers; and 14 Hospitality, Retail and Other Services Managers.   

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
The classification item structure has a set of classification item relationships which are basically adjacency lists. A source classification item has a described relationship to a target list of classification items. The semantic might be, for example, "parentOf", or "contains", etc.</body>
