               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.Code"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Code"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.Code-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Code-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
The characters used as a symbol to designate a category within a codelist or classification. (Formally, a sign for which the signifier is non-linguistic alphanumeric string.)   

Examples 
========== 
The letter M might stand for the category "Male" in the codeList called "Gender".  

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
A non-linguistic alphanumeric string is one which does not correspond to a word in natural language. For use in a codelist. The representation property (value) is expressed as it would be found in a data file. Multiple representations may relate to the same category but should be expressed as separate codes.  It should not be confused with a classification item which is a placeholder for a position in a statistical classification.
</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.Code"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>Code</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Code-identifier"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Code-identifier"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>identifier</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Identifier"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.Code-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Code-identifier-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Code-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Code-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Category"/>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.Code_denotes_Category"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.Code-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#Code-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Notation"/>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.Code_uses_Notation"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.CodeList"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition 
============ 
List of codes and associated categories.  

Examples 
========== 
The codes "M" and "F" could point to "Male" and "Female" categories respectively.  A code list for an occupational classification system like the International Standard Classification of Occupations (ISCO-08: https://www.ilo.org/public/english/bureau/stat/isco/isco08/) could use a classification relation structure to describe a hierarchy (Chief Executives and Administrative and Commercial Managers as subtypes of Managers).   

Explanatory notes 
=================== 
List may be flat or hierarchical. A hierarchical structure may have an indexed order for intended presentation even though the content within levels of the hierarchy are conceptually unordered. For hierarchical structures classification item structure is used to provide additional information on the structure and organization of the categories. Note that a category set can be structured by a classification relation structure without the need for associating any codes with the categories. This allows for the creation of a category set, for example for a response domain, without an associated codelist.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CodeList"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>CodeList</name>
                  <generalization xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-generalization"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-generalization"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
                     <general xmi:idref="cdi.EnumerationDomain"/>
                  </generalization>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-allowsDuplicates"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-allowsDuplicates"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>allowsDuplicates</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#Boolean"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-allowsDuplicates-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-allowsDuplicates-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <defaultValue xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-allowsDuplicates-defaultValue"
                                    xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-allowsDuplicates-defaultValue"
                                    xmi:type="uml:LiteralBoolean">
                        <value>False</value>
                     </defaultValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedAttribute-2"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.CodePosition"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedAttribute-2-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedAttribute-2-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.CodePosition_has_CodeList"/>
                     <aggregation>composite</aggregation>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedAttribute-3"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <isReadOnly>true</isReadOnly>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.Code"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedAttribute-3-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                     <upperValue xmi:id="cdi.CodeList-ownedAttribute-3-upperValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeList-ownedAttribute-3-upperValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                        <value>*</value>
                     </upperValue>
                     <association xmi:idref="cdi.Code_has_CodeList"/>
                     <aggregation>shared</aggregation>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.CodeListStructure"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeListStructure"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Class">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.CodeListStructure-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#CodeListStructure-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
Relation structure of codes within a codelist.

Explanatory notes
===================
Allows for the specification of complex relationships among codes. The code list structure employs a set of code relationips to describe the relationship among concepts. Each code relationship is a one to many description of connections between codes. Together they might commonly describe relationships as complex as a hierarchy.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CodeListStructure"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>CodeListStructure</name>
