                  </ownedLiteral>
                  <ownedLiteral xmi:id="cdi.TableDirectionValues-Rtl"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TableDirectionValues-Rtl"
                                 xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
                     <name>Rtl</name>
                  </ownedLiteral>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.TemporalOperator"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalOperator"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.TemporalOperator-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalOperator-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
Set of control flow operators where the continuation of the execution flow depends on the finalization of one or more preceding activities.

</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.TemporalOperator"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>TemporalOperator</name>
                  <ownedLiteral xmi:id="cdi.TemporalOperator-AndJoin"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalOperator-AndJoin"
                                 xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
                     <name>AndJoin</name>
                  </ownedLiteral>
                  <ownedLiteral xmi:id="cdi.TemporalOperator-AndSplit"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalOperator-AndSplit"
                                 xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
                     <name>AndSplit</name>
                  </ownedLiteral>
                  <ownedLiteral xmi:id="cdi.TemporalOperator-XorJoin"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalOperator-XorJoin"
                                 xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
                     <name>XorJoin</name>
                  </ownedLiteral>
                  <ownedLiteral xmi:id="cdi.TemporalOperator-XorSplit"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalOperator-XorSplit"
                                 xmi:type="uml:EnumerationLiteral">
                     <name>XorSplit</name>
                  </ownedLiteral>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.TemporalRelation"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalRelation"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Enumeration">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.TemporalRelation-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TemporalRelation-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
==========
Set of thirteen Allen's interval relations defined as Contains, Finishes, Meets, Overlaps, Precedes, Starts (and their converses), plus Equals. These are jointly exhaustive and pairwise disjoint binary relations representing temporal relationships between pairs of time intervals.

Explanatory notes
=================
Here are the relations in Allen's interval algebra:

- a precedes b (p) and b is preceded by a (P)
- a meets b (m) and b is met by a (M)
- a overlaps b (o) and b is overlapped by a (O)
- a is finished by b (F) and b finishes a (f)
- a contains B (D) and b is during a (d)
- a starts b (s) and b is started by a (S)
- a and b equal (e) each other
</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.TemporalRelation"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>TemporalRelation</name>
                  <ownedLiteral xmi:id="cdi.TemporalRelation-Contains"
