               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PairedControlledVocabularyEntry"
                                 xmi:type="uml:DataType">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
==========
A tightly bound pair of items from an external controlled vocabulary. The extent property describes the extent to which the parent term applies for the specific case.

Examples
========
When used to assign a role to an actor within a specific activity this term would express the degree of contribution. Contributor with term (role) "Editor" and extent "Lead".

Alternatively the term might be a controlled vocabulary from a list of controlled vocabularies, e.g. the Generic Longitudinal Business Process Model (GLBPM) in a list that could include other business process model frameworks. In this context the extent becomes the name of a business process model task, e.g. "integrate data" from the GLBPM.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>PairedControlledVocabularyEntry</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-extent"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-extent"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>extent</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ControlledVocabularyEntry"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-extent-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-extent-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-term"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#PairedControlledVocabularyEntry-term"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>term</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ControlledVocabularyEntry"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
