                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.TextPositionSelector"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TextPositionSelector"
                                 xmi:type="uml:DataType">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.TextPositionSelector-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TextPositionSelector-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
==========
Describes a range of text by recording the start and end positions of the selection in the object. Position 0 would be immediately before the first character, position 1 would be immediately before the second character, and so on. It is defined accordingly the related selector of the Web Annotation Vocabulary, see https://www.w3.org/TR/annotation-vocab/#textpositionselector.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.TextPositionSelector"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>TextPositionSelector</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.TextPositionSelector-end"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TextPositionSelector-end"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>end</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#Integer"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.TextPositionSelector-start"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TextPositionSelector-start"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>start</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#Integer"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.TimeRole"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TimeRole"
                                 xmi:type="uml:DataType">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.TimeRole-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TimeRole-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
Time-specific role given to a represented variable in the context of a data structure. The specific characterization of the role (e.g. event, valid, transaction, reference, etc.) may be given by a controlled vocabulary.


</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.TimeRole"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>TimeRole</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.TimeRole-time"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TimeRole-time"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>time</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ControlledVocabularyEntry"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.TimeRole-time-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TimeRole-time-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.TypedString"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TypedString"
                                 xmi:type="uml:DataType">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.TypedString-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TypedString-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
TypedString combines a type with content defined as a simple string. May be used wherever a simple string needs to support a type definition to clarify its content.

Examples
==========
Content is a regular expression and the typeOfContent attribute is used to define the syntax of the regular expression content.

Explanatory notes
===================
This is a generic type + string where property name and documentation should be used to define any specification for the content. If international structured string content is required use TypedStructuredString.</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.TypedString"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>TypedString</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.TypedString-content"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TypedString-content"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>content</name>
                     <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType"
                            href="http://www.eclipse.org/uml2/5.0.0/UML/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
                  </ownedAttribute>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.TypedString-typeOfContent"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TypedString-typeOfContent"
                                   xmi:type="uml:Property">
                     <name>typeOfContent</name>
                     <type xmi:idref="cdi.ControlledVocabularyEntry"/>
                     <lowerValue xmi:id="cdi.TypedString-typeOfContent-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#TypedString-typeOfContent-lowerValue"
                                  xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                        <value>0</value>
                     </lowerValue>
                  </ownedAttribute>
               </packagedElement>
               <packagedElement xmi:id="cdi.WebLink"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#WebLink"
                                 xmi:type="uml:DataType">
                  <ownedComment xmi:id="cdi.WebLink-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#WebLink-ownedComment"
                                 xmi:type="uml:Comment">
                     <body>Definition
============
A web site (normally a URL) with information on type of site, privacy flag, and effective dates.

</body>
                     <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.WebLink"/>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <name>WebLink</name>
                  <ownedAttribute xmi:id="cdi.WebLink-effectiveDates"
                                   xmi:uuid="https://www.ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/#WebLink-effectiveDates"
